st is comparing output between runs that have different preconditions. I need to either use separate temp directories for each binary or skip the verbose output comparison for this recursive copy scenario. Looking at the test results, `r2_1_recursive` passes, which tells me the framework must be handling the WorkDir correctly for both binaries. I need to examine the difftest.go implementation to see how it isolates or manages the directories when running both the reference and Go versions.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3833,"cache_read_input_tokens":41047,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3833},"output_tokens":9,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"f2328bfb-f30c-46fd-a083-af24b31ecb76","uuid":"1b735a71-b655-4e56-9378-528cab0049e5"}
